WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.823
- Every time I get in the car,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.813
and I'm thinking,

00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:10.977
"Is this the one that's
gonna beat me to death?"

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.080
- [Mark] Alright, Jackie.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:18.913
- [Jackie] Yes.

00:00:18.913 --> 00:00:19.746
- [Mark] Jackie, where'd you grow up,

00:00:19.746 --> 00:00:21.340
where are you from, originally?

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.310
- [Jackie] Lafayette,
California, raised in Watts.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.143
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:27.040
Did you have both of your
parents when you were a kid?

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.810
- I never knew my father, and, my mom

00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:33.480
abandoned me when I was two years old.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.700
When my grandmother found me,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.840
I had to learn how to walk again

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.253
because I was so malnourished
that I couldn't walk.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.993
So as I grew up, she had a daughter, and,

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.600
I wasn't treated like her daughter.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.770
I beat, her daughter didn't get beat.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.230
I ran away several times.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.140
I always ended up going back.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.640
By the time I was 16, 16-17,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.400
I was raped by my teacher.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.233
Imagine that.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.250
She didn't believe me.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.240
She didn't believe me.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.773
So she sent me to Kaiser.

00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:09.830
- [Mark] To where?
- Kaiser.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.550
It's a mental hospital, Kaiser.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.150
She thought I had a sex problem,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.483
and he said basically the
same thing that she said.

00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:20.527
"I asked for it."

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.610
So I figured if everybody felt that way,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.023
I don't have to be here, why am I here?

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.010
I never felt loved.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.660
I never understood what love was.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.176
(sniffles)

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.190
So I reached out for
love in different ways.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.560
- [Mark] Do you feel
like you were ever loved?

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.360
- I still don't feel like I'm loved.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:51.267
How can I feel loved if I
don't know how to love myself?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.470
Can't nobody do nothing to
me that I do worse to myself.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.453
I treat myself worse than
anybody, anybody ever could,

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.230
because I don't think
I deserve to be happy.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.780
I put myself in deadly
situations on a daily basis.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.930
I don't have people watching my back.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.790
As tiny as I am, I'm not
afraid to walk down the street

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.990
and get in cars with two
or three different men.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.020
I've had guns pointed to my head.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:23.853
I've been beat.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.683
I've been stabbed here, I almost died.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.813
I didn't know this was gonna
be this hard, I'm sorry.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.250
And then on top of that,
I started getting high,

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.330
and that didn't help either.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.580
(sniffles)

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.763
Sometimes I wonder why am I here?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.930
There's no purpose for me here.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.510
Why did God put me here?

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.860
Everybody that come in
contact with me, I hurt.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.760
So what's my point?

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.140
- [Mark] Your childhood was so rough that

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.160
you never learned to love yourself.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.080
- I never felt it, so I
don't know what it is.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.323
For some reason I think
it's supposed to hurt.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.100
- [Mark] Do you think that's what maybe

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:36.750
attracts a lot of women
to this lifestyle is...

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.350
- Low self-esteem, and
they don't know how...

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.500
They don't think they deserve to be happy.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.590
At least that's what I feel.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.910
I can't talk for nobody else,

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.440
but I feel that I don't
deserve to be happy.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.273
- [Mark] Because this lifestyle

00:03:50.273 --> 00:03:53.009
kind of provides treatment that's...

00:03:53.009 --> 00:03:55.000
- And then when I get high,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.390
it takes that thought
away for a little while,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.400
and I forget about it,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.339
but then when I come down
and have to get high,

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:02.620
more (indistinct) to
get high all over again

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.193
to make the thoughts go away.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.440
It's like suicidal.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.920
I was just too scared to do it that way,

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.723
so I do it different ways.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.957
Cause in the back of my mind,
I really do want to die.

00:04:17.658 --> 00:04:18.825
I want to die.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.147
- [Mark] You started working
the street at what age?

00:04:23.147 --> 00:04:26.770
- 17.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.100
- [Mark] I'm sure you've
had bad experiences.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:29.933
- Yeah.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.180
But it was weird though,

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.400
because when I started,

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.305
I was hungry, and I was
just walking down...

00:04:36.305 --> 00:04:37.630
Where was I?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.463
Somewhere on Broadway.

00:04:38.463 --> 00:04:40.273
And I was just walking down the street,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.340
and this guy, he seemed real nice.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.370
He said, "You need a ride?"

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.940
So I got in the car.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.730
He says, now I never done this,

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:51.107
he says, "I've got $24,
can we do something?"

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.280
I said, "Yeah."

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.580
And it was quick and easy.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.290
Next few times was quick and easy,

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:02.573
but then I met that one
person that wanted to beat me.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.680
Took the money back...

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.160
When you're...I kept doing it.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.110
And I'm still doing it.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.557
I'm 54 years old.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:13.700
- [Mark] You still working?

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:14.533
- Yeah.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.360
Eventually something has to change.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.108
I'm getting too old, but
I don't know nothing else.

00:05:24.108 --> 00:05:26.690
- [Mark] Is this all you've ever done?

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.210
- All I've ever done.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.800
I love to read though.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.803
I love to read.

00:05:31.846 --> 00:05:34.311
I'm very intelligent.

00:05:34.311 --> 00:05:36.323
I'm an intelligent, stupid person.

00:05:38.143 --> 00:05:39.643
- [Mark] Do you have children?

00:05:40.693 --> 00:05:42.630
- I have many children.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.463
- [Mark] Three?

00:05:43.463 --> 00:05:45.540
- I have a gang of children.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.850
- [Mark] How many?

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.850
- I have nine living and three deceased.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.280
- [Mark] So you lost some.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.683
- I lost three at one time.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.537
They died in a car accident.

00:05:56.537 --> 00:05:57.370
- [Mark] I'm sorry.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.933
- Yeah, so altogether I have 12.

00:06:04.014 --> 00:06:07.650
All of them drug addicted but one.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:08.483
- [Mark] All of what?

00:06:08.483 --> 00:06:11.032
- All of them were born with
drugs in they system but one.

00:06:11.032 --> 00:06:11.865
- [Mark] Oh really?

00:06:11.865 --> 00:06:13.747
- Yeah, I never raised none of them.

00:06:13.747 --> 00:06:15.728
- [Mark] And you're still using today?

00:06:15.728 --> 00:06:17.394
- Yeah.
- [Mark] Crack?

00:06:17.394 --> 00:06:19.227
- Yeah.
- [Mark] Okay.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.870
- Can you imagine what your
life might've been like

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.943
if you had loving parents
and a good childhood?

00:06:29.495 --> 00:06:30.700
- [Jackie] I see other people like that,

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.094
but I just can't see me that way.

00:06:32.094 --> 00:06:32.996
- [Mark] Can't picture it.

00:06:32.996 --> 00:06:34.163
- [Jackie] No.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.367
- [Mark] That's a shame.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:48.093
- [Jackie] It's a short
story, but it's mine.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.830
I don't know what else to do.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.520
- [Mark] I'm sure it gets you depressed.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.370
- [Jackie] Yeah, I take
depression medication.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.603
- [Mark] You do?
- [Jackie] Yeah.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.820
Cause I get depressed, I get suicidal, so,

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.308
They don't want me getting depressed.

00:07:05.308 --> 00:07:06.270
- [Mark] Have you tried suicide?

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.193
- [Jackie] Yeah, that's
why I stopped taking,

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:08.863
I don't take pills anymore.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:12.560
I don't like pain that way, so.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:13.947
I'm scared of blood, so.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:18.053
I walked out in front of a car before.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.550
Then (indistinct).

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:24.923
I'm still trying to
figure out, why am I here?

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.380
Then they say he don't make mistakes,

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.823
but I don't believe
that cause I think I am.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.120
- [Mark] And the guys who pick
you up, tell me about them.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.730
- [Jackie] Oh, you got
a bunch of weird ones.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.470
You got some nice ones, you do.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.883
But you get more strange
ones than you're getting.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.320
You got some that are nice, and
they just want your company.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.370
And you have some that want to be dominant

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.470
and want you to crawl around on the floor.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.940
And then you just got
some weird ones that when,

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:01.680
once you, they want to piss all on you.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.543
Or, watch them shit in a paper
bag and smear it all on them.

00:08:05.543 --> 00:08:07.753
It's weird, I do have some weird ones.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.123
- [Mark] What's the hardest
part of this lifestyle for you?

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:24.453
- Right now?

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:30.643
Every time I get in the car,

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.139
and thinking is this the one

00:08:36.139 --> 00:08:37.783
that's going to beat me to death?

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.050
And the weird part about it though,

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.240
I don't know if that's
the hard part or not

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.990
because I smile and get in the car.

00:08:47.253 --> 00:08:48.641
- [Mark] You do it anyway.

00:08:48.641 --> 00:08:50.058
- I do it anyway.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.230
That's what they say insanity is, right?

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:58.680
Doing the same thing
expecting different results.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:03.717
- [Mark] What was the
best time of your life?

00:09:09.057 --> 00:09:10.593
- When I had my first baby.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.390
When I first looked at him,

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.300
I tell you, I was happy then,

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:22.110
that two seconds, when they
put the baby right here.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:23.507
And you look down (indistinct).

00:09:24.853 --> 00:09:27.503
Then I said, "What the hell
am I gonna do with this?"

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:32.260
It's crazy.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.880
I like the way it feels when pregnant.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.330
I like the fact something's
growing inside of me.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.580
But then when they come out,

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.257
I don't know do it with only one of them.

00:09:41.257 --> 00:09:42.470
- [Mark] Did you raise your kids?

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.680
- No.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.800
- [Mark] Who raised them?

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:47.340
- I raised my first
child for like two weeks.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.940
I can't do it mentally, I can't.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.963
So, the system,

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.023
family, couple fathers.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.450
One is a couple of them.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.350
I don't even know what they look like.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:09.843
I seen them, when they took them out,

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.000
but I couldn't tell you
what they look like.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.450
If they walked up and
stood in front of me,

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:18.027
I couldn't tell you what they looked like.

00:10:21.291 --> 00:10:22.124
- [Mark] How do you think your years

00:10:22.124 --> 00:10:23.950
of working the streets has changed you?

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.423
- I still try to be a nice person.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:33.110
I still say just cause I'm in the streets,

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.750
the streets don't have to be in me.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:39.180
I still try to treat people
the way I want to be treated,

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.513
but there's a flip side.

00:10:42.452 --> 00:10:43.732
There's people (indistinct)

00:10:43.732 --> 00:10:45.613
I can be the nicest person you wanna meet,

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.410
until you draw first blood.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.310
Then it's my turn.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:52.853
I'm very patient.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.493
You might not never know it's
me, but I'm gonna get you.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:02.640
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:05.880
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:07.280
you've learned in your life?

00:11:09.692 --> 00:11:12.260
- [Jackie] Whatever you
do, no matter what it is...

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:14.640
You gonna be a dope head?

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.577
Be the best dope head you can be.

00:11:16.577 --> 00:11:17.730
And you gonna be a hooker?

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:19.623
Be the best hooker you can be.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.760
Don't half step in nothing.

00:11:25.948 --> 00:11:28.659
That don't make sense to you, does it?

00:11:28.659 --> 00:11:30.492
Does it?
- [Mark] Okay.

00:11:31.497 --> 00:11:35.380
- This is all I know, so, I'm
gonna be the best I can be.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.263
Put your best foot forward.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.433
- [Mark] Alright, Jackie.

00:11:40.433 --> 00:11:42.240
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.073
- Thank you.

00:11:43.073 --> 00:11:44.050
Can I go now?

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.273
- [Mark] You're beautiful.

00:11:47.487 --> 00:11:48.530
(chuckles)

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:49.907
I think you're beautiful!

